# Scorpion Leather Studio

Read @AGENTS.md before substantial work.

Also treat these files as source-of-truth contracts:
- @docs/ARCHITECTURE.md
- @docs/PRODUCT-SCHEMA.md
- @docs/ASSET-MANIFEST.md
- @docs/3D-ASSET-STANDARD.md
- @docs/SHOPIFY-INTEGRATION.md
- @docs/MVP-ACCEPTANCE.md
- @docs/DEVELOPMENT-PLAN.md

## Required behavior

- Preserve separation between domain state, pricing, fitting, renderer, UI, assets, and Shopify.
- Do not put product business rules inside presentation components.
- Keep product configuration data-driven.
- Keep Three.js objects out of canonical business state.
- Do not make Shopify variant explosion the configuration model.
- Do not trust browser-calculated totals as the final production authority.
- Do not couple runtime behavior to placeholder mesh names.
- Prefer deterministic mechanical animation over decorative animation.
- Treat mobile performance as a release requirement.
- Do not claim tests or browser checks were performed unless you actually ran them.

When a requested change conflicts with a repository contract, flag the conflict and update the contract deliberately rather than silently bypassing it.
